menu "WiFi Dap TCP backend (CMSIS-DAP over TCP)"

    config BIRDIEBOT_DAP_TCP_ENABLE
        bool "Enable the CMSIS-DAP over TCP backend (OpenOCD cmsis-dap backend tcp)"
        default n
        help
            Listen on TCP 3241 and serve one debugger at a time with the
            CMSIS-DAP TCP frame format shared by OpenOCD's cmsis-dap TCP
            backend and the XRDAP probes (8-byte header "DAP\0" + u16
            little-endian length + type + reserved, then the CMSIS-DAP
            packet).  Frame format, state machine and host tests:
            docs/dap-tcp-backend.md.

            M3 SKELETON: the server reads frames but does not run the DAP
            engine.  Every request is handed to the weak hook
            birdiebot_dap_tcp_execute(); the default implementation reports
            "not wired" and the server closes the connection.  Wire the hook
            (docs/dap-tcp-backend.md section 7) before enabling this in a
            release build.

            The transport is plain text and unauthenticated: enable it only on
            a trusted LAN.

            Default: n - the shipped USBIP / WebSocket-DAP / elaphureLink
            behaviour is unchanged and nothing listens on 3241.

    config BIRDIEBOT_DAP_TCP_PORT
        int "Listening port"
        depends on BIRDIEBOT_DAP_TCP_ENABLE
        range 1024 65535
        default 3241
        help
            TCP port of the CMSIS-DAP backend.  3241 matches the XRDAP probes;
            OpenOCD selects it with `cmsis-dap tcp port 3241`.  The port is
            free in this firmware (the removed corsacOTA service used it), and
            the USBIP / WebSocket-DAP / elaphureLink front-end keeps 3240.

    config BIRDIEBOT_DAP_TCP_CORE
        int "Core affinity of the DAP TCP server task"
        depends on BIRDIEBOT_DAP_TCP_ENABLE
        range 0 1
        default 1 if SOC_CPU_CORES_NUM > 1
        default 0
        help
            Core that runs the DAP TCP server task.  On the dual-core
            ESP32-S3, core 1 places the socket task next to the DAP task
            (BIRDIEBOT_DAP_TASK_PRIORITY) and the USBIP front-end, which
            minimizes the hand-off latency to SWD.

            Single-core targets (ESP32, ESP32-C3, ESP32-C5) must use 0: pinning
            a task to core 1 trips the FreeRTOS core-id assert.

    config BIRDIEBOT_DAP_TCP_TASK_STACK
        int "Stack size of the DAP TCP server task (bytes)"
        depends on BIRDIEBOT_DAP_TCP_ENABLE
        range 3072 8192
        default 4096
        help
            The session buffers (~2 KiB) are static, so the stack only covers
            lwIP socket calls and the frame handling.  4096 matches the USBIP
            front-end task on the S3; raise it if a stack overflow is observed.

    config BIRDIEBOT_DAP_TCP_TASK_PRIORITY
        int "Priority of the DAP TCP server task"
        depends on BIRDIEBOT_DAP_TCP_ENABLE
        range 5 24
        default 14
        help
            FreeRTOS priority of the DAP TCP server task; 14 matches the USBIP
            front-end (BIRDIEBOT_USBIP_TCP_PRIORITY).  The DAP command task
            runs higher (16), so an accepted request still gets the SWD
            bit-banging time slice promptly.

endmenu
